    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled within the highly sought-after Bayview development just off Killiney Hill Road, 8 Bayview Glen presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a beautifully positioned home in one of South Dublin's most desirable coastal settings. Overlooking the expansive green area to the front, and with Killiney Beach and Killiney DART Station nearby, the property combines convenience, connectivity and an enviable coastal lifestyle. Approached via a private driveway providing valuable off-street parking for two cars, the attractive part brick façade creates an appealing first impression, while well-defined boundary walls enhance both privacy and security.\n\nThe accommodation is bright, welcoming and thoughtfully arranged for modern family living. An entrance porch leads to a light-filled reception hall, which sets the tone for the accommodation throughout. At ground floor level, a spacious dual-aspect living and dining room enjoys excellent natural light and provides ample space for both everyday living and entertaining. The kitchen/breakfast room forms a practical and sociable heart to the home and opens directly to the rear garden.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The layout will appeal to a broad range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, young families and those seeking a well-located home within easy reach of an excellent range of amenities.\n\nThe rear garden enjoys a highly desirable westerly orientation, allowing residents to make the most of the afternoon and evening sunshine. It provides an ideal setting for outdoor dining, relaxation and entertaining. Foundations have also been put in place for a permanent structure, offering excellent potential for a garden shed, home office, gym or a variety of other uses, subject to the necessary requirements.\n\nThe location is a particular highlight, with Killiney DART Station approximately a 15-minute walk away, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and the surrounding coastal suburbs. Killiney Beach lies just beyond the green, offering scenic walks and recreational opportunities throughout the year. Excellent transport links are also readily accessible, with the N11, M50 and LUAS all within a short drive.\n\nThe vibrant coastal town of Dalkey and Sandycove village, together with nearby Dún Laoghaire, offer an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques, schools and leisure facilities, all within easy reach."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorched Entrance - 1.9m x 1.1m\nopens through to the\n\nEntrance Hall - 3.85m x 1.95m\nwith understairs storage, ceiling coving, enclosed fuse board and alarm panel\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 4.35m x 3.5m + 3.8m x 2.9m\ndual aspect with ceiling coving, open fireplace with white marble mantle surround and inset, and brass inset, double doors out to the rear garden and opens through to the\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 3.9m x 2.5m\nwith door out to the rear garden, a range of fitted cupboards and units, sink unit, work surfaces, tiled splashbacks, houses the Vokera gas fired boiler, provision for an electric cooker with extractor fan over, provision for a dishwasher, provision for fridge and wine rack\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - \nwith large skylight, access to the attic and shelved hot press with dual immersion and timer\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.8m x 3.4m\nwith a range of fitted wardrobes and vanity area\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.1m x 2.9m\nwith a range of fitted wardrobes and vanity area\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.7m x 2.4m\n\n\nBathroom - 1.8m x 2.1m\nwith Jacuzzi bath with Mira Elite SE electric shower over, w.c., wash hand basin, heated towel rail, fully tiled walls and tiled floor\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Bright and spacious accommodation extending to approximately 89sq.m. (958sq.ft.) </li><li>Private, low-maintenance rear garden with foundations in place for a permanent structure, subject to the necessary requirements.</li><li>Double glazed windows </li><li>Gas-fired central heating </li><li>Off-street parking for two cars </li><li>Fitted carpets and curtains included in the sale </li><li>Short walk to Killiney DART Station and Killiney Beach </li><li>Close to a wide range of amenities and leisure facilities </li><li>Excellent transport connectivity (M50, N11, LUAS) </li><li>Within the catchment area of highly regarded primary and secondary schools including Glenageary Killiney National School, St. Joseph of Cluny and Holy Child Killiney</li><li>Nearby amenities include Killiney Shopping Centre, SuperValu, Killiney Hill Park and Killiney Golf Club</ul>"
      },
